            <ArticleTitle>Keep an eye out for tubulo-interstitial nephritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>523-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute tubulo-interstitial nephritis and uveitis syndrome (TINU) is a rare disease, generally presenting in young women. We describe a 16-year-old Turkish girl with aspecific symptoms and elevated serum creatinine. Further, she complained about a burning pain in her left eye. Renal biopsy revealed acute TIN. Other conditions were excluded and TINU was diagnosed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
